# Project O.L.I.V.I.A.

**Optimized Lightweight Intelligent Vehicle for Immediate Aid** was a fully autonomous fixed-wing UAV developed by **Fly Mi – Politecnico di Milano** for the **IMechE UAS Challenge 2025**.

The aircraft was designed to transport and autonomously release a **2.5 kg payload** over a mission of approximately **15 km**.

## My Role

**Chief Technology Officer — 50+ member programme**

I was responsible for the end-to-end technical coordination of the project across five technical departments. My work included:

- translating mission requirements into aircraft and system architecture;
- coordinating design, manufacturing, procurement, integration and verification;
- aircraft-level integration of aerodynamics, structures, propulsion, electronics, controls and operations;
- planning progressive SITL/HITL, demonstrator and full-aircraft testing;
- supervising 150+ hours of flight-test activity across three aircraft;
- flight readiness, safety processes, anomaly investigation and return-to-flight decisions;
- technical coordination with sponsors and external partners.

The team achieved **3rd place overall among 42 teams**, won the **Safety Award**, and was the best-finishing Italian team.

> **Public-material note:** O.L.I.V.I.A. includes substantial non-public engineering work. Only selected material suitable for public distribution is included; additional design data, analyses, software and internal documentation cannot be shared here.
